      "id": 151825,
      "name": "arenson9",
      "username": "arenson9",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-12-24T17:50:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Growing up Jewish, the closest I had to Christmas traditions was to go see a movie and get Chineese food, since everything else was closed.</p><p>Since marrying a Christian, our Christmas tradition became to travel to her parents' house and celebrate with family: A big mean, that served as leftovers for most of the rest of the week, plus, when our niecephews were little, opening presents from under the tree.</p><p>Her family's get togethers have moved to the summer, though, now, so we're left to create new traditions. So far our Christmas tradition has been to go see a Star Wars movie two days before Christmas with plans to see it again on Christmas day.</p>",
      "post_number": 4,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:30:49.904Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
