      "raw": "<p>Growing up Jewish, the closest I had to Christmas traditions was to go see a movie and get Chineese food, since everything else was closed.</p><p>Since marrying a Christian, our Christmas tradition became to travel to her parents&#39; house and celebrate with family: A big mean, that served as leftovers for most of the rest of the week, plus, when our niecephews were little, opening presents from under the tree.</p><p>Her family&#39;s get togethers have moved to the summer, though, now, so we&#39;re left to create new traditions. So far our Christmas tradition has been to go see a Star Wars movie two days before Christmas with plans to see it again on Christmas day.</p>",
